MongoDB (NoSQL - Document Store)
MongoDB is like a filing cabinet, where each file (document) can have different types of information inside.

Stores data in JSON-like documents instead of rows and columns like MySQL.

Uses B+ Tree indexes, just like MySQL, to quickly search for documents in its storage.

